From 95c8e74374e6081900fa0599f1803d70c2407b7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:32:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(android): add a pinch command

Adds `pinch: {scale, point, duration}`: two fingers move apart (scale
above 1, zooming in) or together around a point, "50%,50%" by default,
or pixels as "x,y". The scale defaults to 2 and the duration to 500 ms.

`adb shell input` and `sendevent` (without root) send one finger only,
so the Android driver's instrumentation moves the two pointers with
UiAutomator's performTwoPointerGesture, through a new `pinch` rpc. The
fingers end at most 40% of the screen's shorter side apart, less near a
side edge, so they land around the point (inside a split view's pane),
and stay at least a tenth of that apart whatever the scale. Other
drivers fail with an unsupported-command error.
